1
00:00:11,300 --> 00:00:17,540
Aiming for the sunset floating
over the Nakagawa River,

2
00:00:18,060 --> 00:00:24,660
when I kick a pebble,
even my shoes go flying.

3
00:00:25,780 --> 00:00:32,960
Wondering if I should take a chance on it,

4
00:00:32,960 --> 00:00:39,140
they laughed at me for still being a kid.

5
00:00:39,910 --> 00:00:44,200
Even if I somehow stir up some energy,

6
00:00:44,200 --> 00:00:46,100
Katsushika Kameari

7
00:00:46,100 --> 00:00:49,280
even a yawn changes nothing.

8
00:00:49,280 --> 00:00:53,180
The town's streets feel strangely gentle.

9
00:00:54,660 --> 00:01:07,440
From the pointed-hat water canteen,
the sunset falls across the great sky.

10
00:01:10,880 --> 00:01:21,060
Tomorrow will end just like this, won't it?
Katsushika Shibamata, losing happiness once again.

11
00:01:29,460 --> 00:01:31,640
Torrent Yagata Mune Panic

12
00:01:45,420 --> 00:01:47,300
Come on, come on, come on!

13
00:01:48,020 --> 00:01:49,360
What'll it be, Ryo-san?

14
00:01:49,360 --> 00:01:52,980
It's a limited edition kit, so if you miss it now,
you'll never get another one.

15
00:01:53,400 --> 00:01:54,080
Put it on my tab.

16
00:01:55,060 --> 00:01:55,880
Absolutely not!

17
00:01:56,120 --> 00:01:58,920
You still owe me for last
year and the year before!

18
00:01:58,920 --> 00:02:00,180
Cash only!

19
00:02:01,200 --> 00:02:03,160
If it's credit, then just go home already.

20
00:02:03,160 --> 00:02:05,920
Plenty of people want to get their hands on it,
you know.

21
00:02:05,920 --> 00:02:09,020
Damn it, taking advantage of me like this!

22
00:02:09,500 --> 00:02:12,100
Well, if it's come to this

23
00:02:12,100 --> 00:02:14,100
Gah! Take it, you thief!

24
00:02:14,540 --> 00:02:15,580
Thanks for your business!

25
00:02:16,440 --> 00:02:18,920
Haha! Yes! I did it! I did it!

26
00:02:19,900 --> 00:02:22,232
Hmm

27
00:02:22,282 --> 00:02:24,400
Hmm, hmm

28
00:02:26,960 --> 00:02:29,740
I should have just paid half, after all.

29
00:02:30,280 --> 00:02:32,120
I went and spent all my money.

30
00:02:32,880 --> 00:02:35,540
How am I going to make it
through until next payday?

31
00:02:36,000 --> 00:02:38,660
Well, I'll be skipping the company trip this time,
that's for sure.

32
00:02:41,960 --> 00:02:43,260
A company trip

33
00:02:44,700 --> 00:02:45,580
Alright!

34
00:02:49,340 --> 00:02:52,220
For the upcoming Katsushika
station staff trip,

35
00:02:52,940 --> 00:02:54,060
you're going to be the organizer?

36
00:02:55,060 --> 00:02:56,880
Are you serious, Ryo-chan?

37
00:02:57,460 --> 00:03:00,700
Yes, I'm serious.
In the spirit of volunteering,

38
00:03:00,700 --> 00:03:04,280
I've decided to go all out for everyone.

39
00:03:04,960 --> 00:03:07,320
Just like you, Lord Ryo. How admirable.

40
00:03:07,980 --> 00:03:11,620
But last year you were complaining so
much that the travel costs were too high.

41
00:03:12,760 --> 00:03:17,160
Yes, and when you were the organizer,
you said you could only drink half the sake.

42
00:03:17,160 --> 00:03:21,520
Senpai, you're not up to
something shady again, are you?

43
00:03:21,520 --> 00:03:22,460
Gulp!

44
00:03:24,020 --> 00:03:27,280
Wrong! Listen, think back!
Last year's company trip!

45
00:03:27,640 --> 00:03:30,040
The time the Chief handled the organizing!

46
00:03:31,100 --> 00:03:35,760
Who in their right mind goes to an
amusement park on a Sunday day off?

47
00:03:36,220 --> 00:03:39,240
We spent half a day there
and only got to ride two rides!

48
00:03:39,720 --> 00:03:41,393
And the meal afterward, too,

49
00:03:41,443 --> 00:03:44,420
the portions were tiny, it tasted awful,
and there was no dessert!

50
00:03:44,740 --> 00:03:47,060
And then there was the
karaoke contest at the end!

51
00:03:47,520 --> 00:03:51,300
There was only one song by Kasuga Hachigoro,
my favorite singer,

52
00:03:52,460 --> 00:03:56,220
you broke the mic, we got thrown out of the place,
and not one good thing came of it.

53
00:03:56,420 --> 00:03:59,930
The mic broke because Ryo-chan
sang at the top of his lungs,

54
00:03:59,980 --> 00:04:03,540
and we didn't get thrown out
because Ryo-chan went on a rampage.

55
00:04:03,820 --> 00:04:06,329
Naive! Anticipating that I'd
sing at the top of my lungs,

56
00:04:06,379 --> 00:04:09,240
a great organizer would have known that.

57
00:04:09,460 --> 00:04:11,620
No normal person could be
expected to know that much.

58
00:04:13,080 --> 00:04:19,520
Naive! Far too naive, Nakagawa! Only someone who plans for
every possible situation deserves to be called a great organizer.

59
00:04:20,460 --> 00:04:24,440
Basically, leaving the organizing to
the Chief was the root of the mistake.

60
00:04:24,440 --> 00:04:28,740
Amusement park, meal,
karaoke: it's a totally standard course.

61
00:04:28,740 --> 00:04:30,920
There's not a shred of style in it.

62
00:04:30,920 --> 00:04:35,280
Someone as stiff, dim-witted, and hardheaded
as him could never organize anything!

63
00:04:36,340 --> 00:04:38,060
No, well, what I meant was...

64
00:04:41,080 --> 00:04:41,740
Chief

65
00:04:42,840 --> 00:04:45,220
I understand what you're trying to say.

66
00:04:46,180 --> 00:04:49,220
So you're saying you won't attend the upcoming company trip,
is that it?

67
00:04:49,220 --> 00:04:50,800
That's not it.

68
00:04:50,800 --> 00:04:53,200
I'm saying I'll be the organizer.

69
00:04:53,200 --> 00:04:55,540
There's no way I'd let you do it.

70
00:04:55,540 --> 00:04:56,740
I can do it.

71
00:04:56,740 --> 00:04:59,180
With a budget of 5,000 yen per person,
better than the Chief's

72
00:04:59,180 --> 00:05:01,880
I'll make a trip that's 100 times more fun.

73
00:05:02,640 --> 00:05:03,860
There's no way you could!

74
00:05:04,360 --> 00:05:05,160
I can.

75
00:05:05,160 --> 00:05:08,100
I can.

76
00:05:08,100 --> 00:05:09,100
Can't.

77
00:05:09,100 --> 00:05:09,900
Can.

78
00:05:09,900 --> 00:05:10,500
Can't.

79
00:05:10,500 --> 00:05:12,000
Good luck, Ryo-san!

80
00:05:12,000 --> 00:05:13,300
What do you mean, "can"?

81
00:05:15,220 --> 00:05:16,858
Let me try! But in return,

82
00:05:16,908 --> 00:05:19,507
if the trip is even slightly boring,

83
00:05:19,557 --> 00:05:21,660
you'll cover the entire cost yourself!

84
00:05:22,120 --> 00:05:22,960
Please!

85
00:05:24,720 --> 00:05:27,988
Fine. But if people enjoy it enough,

86
00:05:28,038 --> 00:05:31,040
you'll cancel my reprimand letter.

87
00:05:32,080 --> 00:05:33,763
Very well.

88
00:05:33,813 --> 00:05:36,240
Here's everyone's travel
money and the roster.

89
00:05:36,760 --> 00:05:37,840
Gotcha.

90
00:05:43,320 --> 00:05:47,440
A cruise on a cruiser with that budget,
will it be all right?

91
00:05:47,440 --> 00:05:48,800
Leave it to me.

92
00:05:48,800 --> 00:05:51,520
I have connections all over the place.

93
00:05:51,520 --> 00:05:54,000
Well, that's just a sample, anyway.

94
00:05:54,000 --> 00:05:55,860
Then I'll go arrange it right away.

95
00:05:57,360 --> 00:06:00,840
If we charge 1,000 yen per person,
that's a 4,000 yen profit each.

96
00:06:01,580 --> 00:06:02,940
Ryo-chan is so smart.

97
00:06:11,360 --> 00:06:14,580
Dining on a cruiser with a live band playing,
can you believe it?

98
00:06:14,580 --> 00:06:16,880
This year's trip is totally awesome,
isn't it?

99
00:06:17,280 --> 00:06:18,400
Totally, totally.

100
00:06:18,400 --> 00:06:19,860
It's so very "chobe-rig," like.

101
00:06:19,860 --> 00:06:22,620
I've always wanted to ride a cruiser once.

102
00:06:23,000 --> 00:06:25,220
I'd hate it if I got seasick.

103
00:06:25,760 --> 00:06:26,480
Don't worry, you'll be fine.

104
00:06:26,480 --> 00:06:28,140
A cruiser won't rock, you know.

105
00:06:28,140 --> 00:06:28,880
Good morning.

106
00:06:28,880 --> 00:06:30,300
Good morning, Chief.

107
00:06:30,860 --> 00:06:32,400
Morning, morning.

108
00:06:32,400 --> 00:06:33,800
Ohara-kun.

109
00:06:34,480 --> 00:06:37,680
Chief, thank you so much for taking the trouble to come,
despite how busy you are.

110
00:06:37,680 --> 00:06:39,040
Good morning.

111
00:06:39,720 --> 00:06:43,740
No, I hear this trip is quite luxurious.

112
00:06:43,740 --> 00:06:47,000
For a perennial troublemaker like Ryotsu,
it's not a bad plan, is it?

113
00:06:47,000 --> 00:06:47,940
Well, yes.

114
00:06:47,940 --> 00:06:51,440
But you're really sure this
will be all right, Ohara?

115
00:06:51,440 --> 00:06:52,980
It'll be fine.

116
00:06:52,980 --> 00:06:53,700
Probably.

117
00:06:56,560 --> 00:06:58,520
But Ryotsu's late, isn't he?

118
00:06:58,920 --> 00:07:00,780
I heard the guest Chief has already arrived.

119
00:07:01,240 --> 00:07:03,360
He did say the meeting was at ten,
didn't he?

120
00:07:03,360 --> 00:07:05,720
Yeah, but it's worrying.

121
00:07:05,720 --> 00:07:06,074
Hey,

122
00:07:06,124 --> 00:07:10,300
Can we really get a live band on a cruiser
with a budget of 5,000 yen per person?

123
00:07:10,500 --> 00:07:10,960
Yeah, I guess not.

124
00:07:10,960 --> 00:07:13,700
Hey, everyone! Sorry to keep you waiting!

125
00:07:14,340 --> 00:07:16,060
He finally showed up.

126
00:07:16,540 --> 00:07:17,940
Look, look, that ship!

127
00:07:26,280 --> 00:07:27,480
Wow, how lovely!

128
00:07:28,080 --> 00:07:29,220
Wow, that's amazing, senior!

129
00:07:29,380 --> 00:07:32,860
What a lovely cruiser!
It's more than I imagined!

130
00:07:35,720 --> 00:07:37,560
Aaaaaah!

131
00:07:40,580 --> 00:07:45,240
We went too far, didn't we?
This way, this way!

132
00:07:45,770 --> 00:07:49,140
Okay, everyone, this is it!

133
00:07:52,200 --> 00:08:22,080
Eeeeeeeeeeeeeeeeeeeeeeeeeeeeeeeeeeeeeeeeeeeeeeeeeeeeeeeeeeeeeeeeeeeeeeeeeeeeeeeeeeeeeeeeeeeeeeeeeeeeeeeeeeeeeeeeeeeeeeeeeeeeeeeeeeeeeeeeeeeeeeeeeeeeeeeeeeeeeeeeeeeeeeeeeeeeeeeeeeeeeeeeeeeeeeeeeeeeeeeeeeeeeeeeeeeeeeeeeeeeeeeeeeeeeeeeeeeeeeeeeeeeeeeeeeeeeeeeeeeeeeeeeeeeeeeeeeeeeeeeeeeeeeeeeeeeeeee
eeeeeeee ee ee ee

134
00:08:22,140 --> 00:08:22,549
Yes,

135
00:08:22,599 --> 00:08:27,500
so you can sunbathe and enjoy nature
without even leaving your seat.

136
00:08:29,220 --> 00:08:31,040
The tatami must be pretty worn out, too.

137
00:08:31,420 --> 00:08:32,198
Chief,

138
00:08:32,248 --> 00:08:36,060
don't put too much weight there,
the wood's rotten.

139
00:08:36,060 --> 00:08:36,500
What?

140
00:08:38,020 --> 00:08:38,777
Now, now,

141
00:08:38,827 --> 00:08:42,380
don't make such a scary face.
Let's enjoy the trip!

142
00:08:42,380 --> 00:08:44,820
Yo! Five thousand yen for this is a steal!

143
00:08:44,820 --> 00:08:46,880
Chief, in exchange, the food is

144
00:08:46,880 --> 00:08:48,003
That's right, Ohara-kun,

145
00:08:48,053 --> 00:08:51,740
so what if the boat's a dump,
as long as the food is good?

146
00:08:52,140 --> 00:08:54,280
We'll be able to eat fresh fish, right?

147
00:08:54,280 --> 00:09:02,020
Yes, exactly! Fish is all about freshness. Well then,
let's enjoy some fishing right away!

148
00:09:02,440 --> 00:09:03,500
What should we do, I wonder?

149
00:09:04,900 --> 00:09:05,700
What is this?

150
00:09:05,700 --> 00:09:08,900
You said we'd be doing some grand-scale fishing,
didn't you?

151
00:09:09,440 --> 00:09:11,160
Right. That's what I said.

152
00:09:11,160 --> 00:09:17,020
Chief, Nakagawa, Honda, and the mini-patrol girls,
let's all cast our lines!

153
00:09:17,760 --> 00:09:20,840
Hey, Ryo-chan, we're not going fishing!

154
00:09:22,220 --> 00:09:24,180
That's too bad.

155
00:09:24,680 --> 00:09:25,680
What do you mean?

156
00:09:25,680 --> 00:09:29,440
The fish we catch are going to
be the main dish for today's meal.

157
00:09:29,920 --> 00:09:31,380
Then you two get nothing.

158
00:09:31,920 --> 00:09:32,500
What?!

159
00:09:33,280 --> 00:09:34,500
That's not fair!

160
00:09:34,500 --> 00:09:36,780
You catch what you eat yourself.

161
00:09:36,780 --> 00:09:39,580
This is the new way to do a company trip.

162
00:09:40,100 --> 00:09:43,120
If you don't fish,
you'll have to watch everyone else eating the fresh sashimi.

163
00:09:43,120 --> 00:09:44,960
Sitting there with your
fingers in your mouth.

164
00:09:47,800 --> 00:09:49,860
Don't worry, we'll help you.

165
00:09:50,340 --> 00:09:50,700
Yeah.

166
00:09:52,140 --> 00:09:52,600
Hello!

167
00:09:52,600 --> 00:09:53,000
Thank you!

168
00:09:53,620 --> 00:09:54,740
You really are wonderful!

169
00:09:55,640 --> 00:09:57,180
You're not like you, are you?

170
00:09:57,180 --> 00:09:58,760
Anything's fine.

171
00:10:03,000 --> 00:10:06,820
But just standing in the sea breeze feels so nice,
doesn't it.

172
00:10:07,500 --> 00:10:09,520
This kind of thing is pretty good, too.

173
00:10:10,000 --> 00:10:10,960
Here it comes!

174
00:10:12,200 --> 00:10:13,920
This one's a big catch!

175
00:10:15,460 --> 00:10:15,900
There!

176
00:10:19,040 --> 00:10:20,600
Look, I got one!

177
00:10:22,140 --> 00:10:25,040
Ryo-sama, I've got a bite over here too!

178
00:10:25,040 --> 00:10:26,380
Me too.

179
00:10:28,160 --> 00:10:30,700
It's a black sea bream! Nice work, Maria.

180
00:10:31,220 --> 00:10:32,280
I can do it too!

181
00:10:40,520 --> 00:10:42,040
Alright, here it comes!

182
00:10:43,860 --> 00:10:45,760
Everyone, enjoy yourselves!

183
00:10:46,500 --> 00:10:49,620
Honda, all you've caught are gobies!

184
00:10:49,620 --> 00:10:51,860
For some reason,
these are all I keep catching.

185
00:10:52,580 --> 00:10:55,080
Well, whatever.
Goby tempura is tasty, after all.

186
00:10:57,860 --> 00:11:01,200
What is it, Chief?
You haven't caught a thing!

187
00:11:01,660 --> 00:11:03,780
Shut up,
the real fishing hasn't even started yet!

188
00:11:04,380 --> 00:11:07,240
Even the mini-patrol
girls are catching some!

189
00:11:08,120 --> 00:11:11,920
A man of your rank should
be reeling in tuna or whales.

190
00:11:14,540 --> 00:11:16,700
Watch, you swing it like this, see?

191
00:11:17,380 --> 00:11:19,860
Don't be ridiculous,
talking about tuna or whales.

192
00:11:19,860 --> 00:11:21,623
Anyway, Irotsu. You

193
00:11:21,673 --> 00:11:23,940
don't need to catch your own share?

194
00:11:24,040 --> 00:11:25,641
I'm the organizer, after all.

195
00:11:25,691 --> 00:11:28,500
I'll take from what everyone catches.

196
00:11:28,960 --> 00:11:32,240
Being the organizer means a lot of hardship.

197
00:11:32,880 --> 00:11:35,350
Ryo-sama! I'll catch

198
00:11:35,400 --> 00:11:37,020
Ryo-sama's share, I'll do my best!

199
00:11:37,480 --> 00:11:39,370
Never mind that.

200
00:11:39,420 --> 00:11:42,420
If you don't catch a single one,
there won't be any for the Chief.

201
00:11:43,480 --> 00:11:46,520
We paid five thousand yen each,
and we have to catch our own fish to eat.

202
00:11:46,520 --> 00:11:47,940
There, another one's coming!

203
00:11:48,860 --> 00:11:51,580
Not bad, is it, Ohara-kun?

204
00:11:55,180 --> 00:11:56,260
Here it comes!

205
00:11:56,540 --> 00:11:59,180
G-got a big one here!

206
00:11:59,440 --> 00:12:00,540
Ohara, you can do it!

207
00:12:02,240 --> 00:12:03,340
Chief, hang in there!

208
00:12:04,120 --> 00:12:06,120
Come on! Come on! Come on!

209
00:12:06,260 --> 00:12:09,600
Wow, that's amazing!
Chief, you're catching enough for everyone

210
00:12:10,160 --> 00:12:11,640
Forget that, help me!

211
00:12:11,980 --> 00:12:12,360
Yes.

212
00:12:15,360 --> 00:12:19,020
No way, Chief,
there's absolutely no way you're that good.

213
00:12:19,500 --> 00:12:22,680
Eeeeeeh?

214
00:12:26,160 --> 00:12:27,140
Chief!

215
00:12:27,140 --> 00:12:28,340
I did it!

216
00:12:32,040 --> 00:12:33,740
That looks like a ship's rudder, though.

217
00:12:33,740 --> 00:12:35,400
What are you doing, Chief!

218
00:12:35,720 --> 00:12:38,080
Instead of a fish,
you went and caught a rudder!

219
00:12:39,860 --> 00:12:40,732
But, senpai,

220
00:12:40,782 --> 00:12:44,320
that rudder isn't by any
chance from this boat, is it?

221
00:12:45,180 --> 00:12:47,680
Everyone, don't mind us,
please keep fishing!

222
00:12:50,660 --> 00:12:53,740
I can't believe we actually reeled
in this shabby boat's rudder.

223
00:12:53,740 --> 00:12:55,900
Let's hide this somewhere.

224
00:12:57,520 --> 00:12:58,320
Uh-oh.

225
00:13:00,600 --> 00:13:02,620
This isn't funny at all.

226
00:13:02,620 --> 00:13:04,200
That was pretty fun, wasn't it?

227
00:13:04,200 --> 00:13:05,800
Fishing's easy.

228
00:13:05,800 --> 00:13:08,460
No, no, no, everyone, good work...

229
00:13:08,460 --> 00:13:10,540
Come on, come on,
everyone, sit down, sit down.

230
00:13:14,920 --> 00:13:16,040
Chief, over here.

231
00:13:16,040 --> 00:13:17,380
This is the best seat.

232
00:13:17,380 --> 00:13:19,560
Hey, what about the station chief?

233
00:13:19,560 --> 00:13:20,920
How could I sit there?

234
00:13:21,820 --> 00:13:25,360
Don't be so stiff.
Today's a break, isn't it?

235
00:13:25,360 --> 00:13:30,420
Besides, the station chief is a guest. The
guest of honor on this trip is you, Chief.

236
00:13:30,420 --> 00:13:31,120
But...

237
00:13:31,600 --> 00:13:34,680
That's right, Ohara. Don't hold back at all.

238
00:13:36,220 --> 00:13:38,940
But my backside feels cold somehow.

239
00:13:39,700 --> 00:13:41,260
Don't worry about it, don't worry about it.

240
00:13:41,260 --> 00:13:47,320
Listen, Chief, no matter what happens, sit tight
and whatever you do, don't move from that spot.

241
00:13:48,360 --> 00:13:49,780
Everyone,
give the Chief a round of applause.

242
00:14:04,280 --> 00:14:05,120
Delicious!

243
00:14:07,280 --> 00:14:09,200
The goby tempura is good too.

244
00:14:14,600 --> 00:14:16,680
Chief, if you don't mind, I'll join in too.

245
00:14:16,680 --> 00:14:19,220
Is everybody having a good time?

246
00:14:22,860 --> 00:14:25,086
Come on, go right ahead and help yourselves!

247
00:14:25,136 --> 00:14:27,280
There's plenty of sake, so don't hold back.

248
00:14:27,720 --> 00:14:29,225
Now, the moment you've all been waiting for.

249
00:14:29,275 --> 00:14:32,560
A karaoke contest with
a luxurious live band!

250
00:14:42,780 --> 00:14:44,500
A-aren't you Mr. Sendo?

251
00:14:45,020 --> 00:14:45,464
Yes.

252
00:14:45,514 --> 00:14:49,140
Back in the day, I did a
song-and-comedy routine at Asakusa Rock.

253
00:14:50,920 --> 00:14:52,660
What's going on with the boat arrangements?

254
00:14:52,660 --> 00:14:56,360
Don't worry, it's on autopilot.

255
00:14:56,360 --> 00:14:58,000
Autopilot.

256
00:14:58,000 --> 00:15:00,840
Such state-of-the-art
equipment on this boat?

257
00:15:00,840 --> 00:15:02,480
Somehow I'm worried.

258
00:15:02,480 --> 00:15:03,980
I'll go check.

259
00:15:03,980 --> 00:15:06,780
Chief, don't move, don't move!

260
00:15:07,320 --> 00:15:08,160
Thud!

261
00:15:08,160 --> 00:15:10,820
What is this idiot thing?

262
00:15:10,820 --> 00:15:14,320
Chief, no,
I told you not to move from there!

263
00:15:15,200 --> 00:15:15,920
Ryotsu!

264
00:15:18,560 --> 00:15:19,440
Senpai.

265
00:15:23,180 --> 00:15:26,040
Senpai, at this rate we're going to sink!

266
00:15:26,560 --> 00:15:26,780
What?

267
00:15:28,080 --> 00:15:29,680
Use a bucket to get the key out!

268
00:15:32,440 --> 00:15:33,320
They're going to notice.

269
00:15:41,620 --> 00:15:42,500
Not like that.

270
00:15:50,820 --> 00:15:51,960
Do something!

271
00:15:51,960 --> 00:15:52,820
Ryotsu!

272
00:16:15,760 --> 00:16:17,060
We're finished over here.

273
00:16:17,460 --> 00:16:18,760
Good work, everyone.

274
00:16:18,760 --> 00:16:22,180
Honestly, look what's happened
to our sightseeing boat.

275
00:16:22,720 --> 00:16:26,280
This is all your fault for
arranging this junk boat.

276
00:16:26,280 --> 00:16:28,540
Still, it's rocking an awful lot.

277
00:16:29,940 --> 00:16:31,220
Rain's leaking in.

278
00:16:40,420 --> 00:16:42,620
At this rate,
it's no different from being outside.

279
00:16:44,560 --> 00:16:46,220
What's going on, Ryotsu?

280
00:16:46,220 --> 00:16:49,880
Yes, yes, I've come prepared with
umbrellas for just this kind of situation.

281
00:16:50,340 --> 00:16:51,380
That's thoughtful of you.

282
00:16:51,380 --> 00:16:54,960
But they're rentals,
so it's 200 yen per person.

283
00:16:54,960 --> 00:16:56,180
What did you say?

284
00:16:56,180 --> 00:16:57,240
No way, I don't need one.

285
00:17:04,180 --> 00:17:05,900
It's turning into a storm.

286
00:17:05,900 --> 00:17:07,240
Ugh, seriously.

287
00:17:07,240 --> 00:17:08,240
No way.

288
00:17:08,740 --> 00:17:10,940
Senpai,
we should head back to shore already.

289
00:17:10,940 --> 00:17:12,680
Don't say unnecessary things.

290
00:17:12,680 --> 00:17:15,040
Of course a boat rocks, you idiot.

291
00:17:15,040 --> 00:17:16,200
What's wrong?

292
00:17:17,320 --> 00:17:18,360
I'm starting to get seasick.

293
00:17:18,360 --> 00:17:19,380
Savor it.

294
00:17:19,380 --> 00:17:21,480
That's because you
haven't had enough to drink.

295
00:17:21,960 --> 00:17:24,840
Once you're drunk,
seasickness doesn't matter at all.

296
00:17:26,680 --> 00:17:28,080
This is totally chaotic.

297
00:17:28,560 --> 00:17:29,820
Right, karaoke!

298
00:17:30,340 --> 00:17:32,200
A karaoke contest to forget the storm!

299
00:17:32,200 --> 00:17:34,680
First, the other day,
I was the first to take the stage.

300
00:17:34,680 --> 00:17:38,120
Yujiro Nishihara's "Storm-Calling Gourmet"

301
00:17:39,640 --> 00:17:40,740
That was incredible, wasn't it?

302
00:17:41,560 --> 00:17:43,240
It's seriously a dangerous force.

303
00:17:43,240 --> 00:17:44,900
I'm going too.

304
00:17:44,900 --> 00:17:48,900
A large low-pressure system is
currently approaching the Kanto region.

305
00:17:48,900 --> 00:17:51,520
Vessels at sea, please remain fully alert.

306
00:17:51,520 --> 00:17:54,700
Heavy rain, flood,
and storm warnings are currently in effect.

307
00:17:55,120 --> 00:17:55,860
This is bad.

308
00:17:55,860 --> 00:17:57,720
What on earth is going on?

309
00:17:57,720 --> 00:18:01,060
For 5,000 yen a person,
the service is terrible!

310
00:18:01,060 --> 00:18:03,300
5,000 yen? I paid 1,000 yen.

311
00:18:05,220 --> 00:18:07,280
Come on, have a drink. It's a break.

312
00:18:08,160 --> 00:18:11,220
Bravo! Even in heavy rain or in Taiwan,
they hate it.

313
00:18:11,660 --> 00:18:12,020
Then

314
00:18:12,860 --> 00:18:13,818
You idiot,

315
00:18:13,868 --> 00:18:17,060
If the captain gets drunk,
who's going to steer the boat?

316
00:18:17,440 --> 00:18:19,800
Don't worry, leave it to me.

317
00:18:21,520 --> 00:18:22,960
My nighttime hobby comes in handy.

318
00:18:22,960 --> 00:18:23,600
There.

319
00:18:25,280 --> 00:18:26,920
Baskabaan!

320
00:18:27,140 --> 00:18:29,520
Ryo-chan,
looks like you've done something again.

321
00:18:29,520 --> 00:18:31,100
I don't even want to imagine it.

322
00:18:31,860 --> 00:18:34,360
The boat's going further
and further up the river.

323
00:18:45,760 --> 00:18:47,660
The river's getting narrower.

324
00:18:48,140 --> 00:18:48,980
This is bad!

325
00:18:48,980 --> 00:18:51,240
We've gone from the Sumida
River into the Kanda River!

326
00:18:51,680 --> 00:18:52,000
What?

327
00:18:59,400 --> 00:19:01,260
We're being swept further and further away!

328
00:19:01,860 --> 00:19:05,600
Compared to a ship like that, this boat
is basically a paper leaf boat, isn't it?

329
00:19:18,620 --> 00:19:20,060
The roof's been torn off!

330
00:19:20,720 --> 00:19:23,160
Sorry, senpai,
but going any further is dangerous.

331
00:19:23,160 --> 00:19:25,460
Let's call for rescue.

332
00:19:25,960 --> 00:19:27,380
Hello? It's me.

333
00:19:30,880 --> 00:19:32,220
It's over.

334
00:19:39,460 --> 00:19:41,120
What's going to happen to us?

335
00:19:41,120 --> 00:19:43,200
What will become of us?

336
00:19:43,900 --> 00:19:44,300
No way.

337
00:19:45,040 --> 00:19:45,720
It's not that bad.

338
00:19:45,720 --> 00:19:48,640
You never know what'll happen,
and that's what makes it fun!

339
00:19:48,920 --> 00:19:53,040
This is the real joy of travel!
It's a truly new kind of staff outing!

340
00:19:56,000 --> 00:20:00,100
At this rate we'll capsize!
Bail out the water! Keep your balance!

341
00:20:00,440 --> 00:20:03,420
Renko, move more to the middle!
Nakagawa and Chief, to the left!

342
00:20:03,540 --> 00:20:07,720
Everyone else, split up on both sides and bail out the water!
Hurry, hurry!

343
00:20:08,420 --> 00:20:10,280
It's a miracle it hasn't sunk!

344
00:20:10,680 --> 00:20:13,580
If I make it back alive,
you'd better watch out, Ryotsu!

345
00:20:26,560 --> 00:20:27,520
Look out!

346
00:20:30,400 --> 00:20:31,200
No way, really?

347
00:20:46,380 --> 00:20:48,780
Senpai, the light is red!

348
00:20:49,360 --> 00:20:50,260
Do something about it, Ryotsu!

349
00:20:50,260 --> 00:20:51,180
I know.

350
00:20:57,860 --> 00:20:58,920
That was a close call.

351
00:20:59,300 --> 00:21:00,980
Why did we stop?

352
00:21:00,980 --> 00:21:02,320
That's impossible.

353
00:21:03,720 --> 00:21:04,360
Look.

354
00:21:04,360 --> 00:21:06,720
The screw shaft has broken!

355
00:21:07,660 --> 00:21:08,400
More importantly, senpai,

356
00:21:08,400 --> 00:21:09,820
the current has gotten faster.

357
00:21:10,240 --> 00:21:11,880
It seems we're being sucked into something.

358
00:21:12,560 --> 00:21:12,880
What?

359
00:21:14,280 --> 00:21:15,700
It's the subway entrance!

360
00:21:28,260 --> 00:21:30,200
Aaaaaaah!

361
00:21:30,200 --> 00:21:31,460
Aaaaaaah!

362
00:21:31,460 --> 00:21:31,540
Aaaaaaah!

363
00:21:31,540 --> 00:21:32,260
Aaaaaaah!

364
00:21:33,640 --> 00:21:35,300
Eeeeeeek!

365
00:21:50,680 --> 00:21:52,320
Aaaaaaah!

366
00:21:52,800 --> 00:21:53,640
Yeah, that's true.

367
00:21:53,640 --> 00:21:56,540
Aaaaaaah!

368
00:22:04,400 --> 00:22:05,320
Four of them!

369
00:22:05,320 --> 00:22:12,780
Hey, why the scared face at a time like this?
Come on, have some fun!

370
00:22:13,180 --> 00:22:14,660
Can't you even enjoy that much?

371
00:22:31,960 --> 00:22:34,700
How can you two keep bickering
in a situation like this?

372
00:22:38,960 --> 00:22:39,980
We're outside!

373
00:22:39,980 --> 00:22:41,860
We came out at Ochanomizu.

374
00:22:49,820 --> 00:22:53,260
Aaaaah!

375
00:22:56,120 --> 00:22:57,100
Aaaaah!

376
00:22:58,660 --> 00:22:59,160
Hey.

377
00:23:07,240 --> 00:23:11,620
See, Chief? You didn't get bored for a single second,
did you?

378
00:23:11,620 --> 00:23:21,340
Hey, you idiot! Even if it's Bonofure, with this capacity it's 1,000 yen a head.
It doesn't add up, damn it!

379
00:23:22,040 --> 00:23:30,660
No, no, senpai, Ya-chan!
What is going on? This is, well, that's...

380
00:23:30,660 --> 00:23:31,200
Uh...

381
00:23:31,880 --> 00:23:32,520
Ryotsu!

382
00:23:32,940 --> 00:23:34,414
I thought something was off,

383
00:23:34,464 --> 00:23:36,960
so you were skimming off the trip money after all,
weren't you?

384
00:23:37,320 --> 00:23:38,920
Wh-wait a minute!

385
00:23:41,280 --> 00:23:42,720
My money!

386
00:23:43,020 --> 00:23:43,880
Hey, Ryotsu!

387
00:23:45,120 --> 00:23:45,760
No!

388
00:23:45,960 --> 00:23:48,640
My money, my money!

389
00:23:49,040 --> 00:23:50,360
You big idiot!

390
00:23:50,500 --> 00:23:52,920
Cool your head in the water!

391
00:23:53,160 --> 00:23:55,300
Stop it, Chief!

392
00:23:55,600 --> 00:23:56,960
My money!

393
00:23:57,960 --> 00:23:58,760
No!

394
00:24:04,660 --> 00:24:05,640
Eigo.

395
00:24:05,640 --> 00:24:08,400
Staring at a marriage meeting
photo and sighing like that.

396
00:24:08,400 --> 00:24:10,260
So you've finally decided to get married?

397
00:24:10,640 --> 00:24:11,000
What?

398
00:24:11,400 --> 00:24:13,160
You want me to wreck this omiai?

399
00:24:13,540 --> 00:24:16,420
Then just act like you normally do,
and they'll turn you down.

400
00:24:16,420 --> 00:24:18,140
No, I'm absolutely certain of it.

401
00:24:18,640 --> 00:24:21,180
Next time: Ryo-san's grand plan to marry up.

402
00:24:21,180 --> 00:24:22,100
Thanks, I'm counting on you.

403
00:24:30,660 --> 00:24:42,760
They say I'm a woman who can't fall in love,
but I have so many things I want to do.

404
00:24:44,740 --> 00:24:58,940
I want to ride a motorbike across the wide desert.
I want to be freer than a bird.

405
00:25:00,660 --> 00:25:07,140
A lady's dreams keep changing,
quick as a kaleidoscope.

406
00:25:09,140 --> 00:25:15,200
My heart's longing, sorry, just wait for me.

407
00:25:15,200 --> 00:25:22,220
The panoramic future will soon be dazzling.

408
00:25:23,500 --> 00:25:30,100
You understand, right?
Sorry, just wait for me.

